// lint_waivers.vlt -- Verilator lint waivers for COMMITTED files.
//
// Each waiver below names the single reviewed warning instance it covers.
// Verified 2026-09-27: with these waivers the full design lints with ZERO
// warnings (Verilator 5.053, -Wall). Do NOT broaden a waiver to hide a new
// warning -- fix the RTL instead.
//
// - UNUSEDSIGNAL 'vnwords' (tt_um_pemu_host.v:423): leftover readback-count
//   reg from the VERIFY_IMEM implementation; never read, harmless. This is
//   the only UNUSEDSIGNAL in tt_um_pemu_host.v.
// - SYNCASYNCNET 'rst_n' (tt_um_pemu.v:58): intended reset topology -- the
//   host block uses async-assert/sync-deassert (rst_sync) while the PE
//   samples rst_n synchronously (rst_n_d). Not a bug.
//   (The PE-internal rst_n_d usage is clean; only the top-level crossing fires.)
//
// Usage: verilator --lint-only -Wall --top-module tt_um_pemu \
//            test/lint_waivers.vlt src/tt_um_pemu.v src/tt_um_pemu_pe.v \
//            src/tt_um_pemu_observer.v src/tt_um_pemu_host.v test/sram_bb.v
`verilator_config
lint_off -rule UNUSEDSIGNAL -file "*/tt_um_pemu_host.v"
lint_off -rule SYNCASYNCNET -file "*/tt_um_pemu.v"
